red by her red itchy  peeling skin Stacy continues her regimen  even as her rash worsens and her devoted  husband Keith begs her to stop  no I I'm not talking to the TV  devoted to his wife and supportive of  her Taxidermy hobby Keith is a beacon of  sensibility Keith tries his best to be  supportive of Stacy and her  transformation Journey even as her skin  and mental state get worse finally it  proves to be too much even for him and  he insists that she stopped it's a  suggestion she doesn't appreciate to say  the least after killing her husband and  stuffing poor Keith like one of her  Taxidermy projects her sought after  makeover is finally complete  inspired by an HP Lovecraft story  pikmin's Model tells the tale of Richard  Pikmin played by Crispin Glover who  invites a young artist named William  Thurber played by Ben Barnes to look at  his extremely creepy paintings one of  the paintings depicts a woman a distant  relative in which who killed her husband  and served him to members of her coven  Pikmin taunts Thurber with the painting  and Thurber feels deeply Disturbed  looking at it years later Thurber  continues to be haunted by pikmin's work  plagued by Vivid nightmares including  one in which he walks into the dinner  party from the painting but his own head  is being served as the main course  jumping forward in time we now see  Thurber as an older man and with a wife  and son running his own museum but still  haunted by memories of Pikmin one day  Pikmin unexpectedly returns shocking  Thurber he asked Thurber to come to his  house to see some new paintings in an  attempt to save others from the madness  he suffered Thurber goes alone  oh I know you want to see more new  paintings  [Applause]  but seeing pikmin's new paintings  overwhelms Thurber unable to control his  rage and anguish after all the years of  Torment he shoots Pikmin and burns down  his house the next day when Thurber  takes his family to his Museum he's  shocked to see pikmin's paintings  hanging there and horrifyingly one of  thurber's colleagues Joe standing in  front of the work his eyes gouged out  his wife and child are also looking in a  painting and he makes them stop but it's  too late when Thurber returns home his  wife has gouged her eyes out most  horrifyingly she's also in the middle of  preparing their son's head for dinner  another HP Lovecraft inspired story this  dark fairy tale is brought to life by  Catherine Hardwick director of the  original Twilight it tells the story of  Walter played by Rupert Grint of Harry  Potter Fame a man obsessed with bringing  his twin sister who died when they were  young back to life he becomes part of  the spiritualist society and discovers a  potion that allows him to find his  sister in a place called The Realm of  the Dead Walter even manages to bring  her back to the land of the living  temporarily you brought it back with you  you'll have to Ripple  I just wanted my sister back Walter's  actions anger a witch named kazaya a  Sinister being who also resides in the  Underworld and wants Walter's sister to  stay there with skin like petrified wood  and branch-like hair she resembles a  gnarled Tree in human form her screams  sound like nails on a chalkboard and her  hair is burning embers Furious This  Witch tries to stab poor Walter in the  eye but his ghost sister saves him she  seems different now calmer telling  Walter she's not scared anymore by the  end of the episode poor Walter can't  really say the same for himself  Peter Weller the actor perhaps most  famously known as RoboCop stars in the  viewing as Lionel a wealthy and  eccentric elderly man who invites four  interesting people to his Mansion  there's a psychic named [ __ ] an  astrophysicist named Charlotte a  musician named Randall and a famous  novelist named guy set in the 1970s  debuting benefits from a very  distinctive 70s aesthetic matching this  story Slow Burn intensity as the plot  unfolds it becomes clear why Lionel has 